WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.842
A multilingual site
can use subdirectories,

2
00:00:03.842 --> 00:00:06.164
country domains, subdomains,

3
00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.261
or URL parameters, and Google
ranks none above the others.

4
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.587
General Translation
supports subdirectories,

5
00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:15.827
the practical default
for a shared site.

6
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.401
Subdirectories fit when one
product shares a site and release

7
00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:21.108
process.

8
00:00:21.508 --> 00:00:24.143
Only a country domain
signals a country,

9
00:00:24.143 --> 00:00:26.383
and subdomains allow
separate hosting.

10
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:30.997
Google discourages language
parameters and treats vanity domains

11
00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.411
such as .io as generic.

12
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.353
In gt-next, createNextMiddleware
routes each locale under a

13
00:00:38.353 --> 00:00:42.659
path prefix, and pathConfig
maps localized slugs.

14
00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:45.531
Your team now ships
French with each release.
